# Description of the arches and joints in 01a-julien-delannoy-10-left.png (30 September 2026)

Written from two 4x zoomed crops of the reference at full resolution (1920 px = 4 tiles, so a tile is 480 px). Everything below is what the image shows, not what a model assumes.

## The arch (the ring between two dished regions)

- 30 September 2026 : it is a **cut wall**, as if the tile were laser cut. Seen from the camera (which is a perspective camera, not a pure top view) the wall appears as a **flat band of exposed clay, tan ochre, about #a78c5c** with a slightly more orange centre. Its width is about 8 to 10 px at 1920 where the wall faces the camera and it shrinks to a **hairline of 1 px** where it does not (near the tile junctions the arch is only a thin pale line).
- 30 September 2026 : the band is bordered on **both sides by a thin pale cream line of about 1 px** (near white, #d9cfb0 to #efe6cc): one at the top edge of the wall (rim of the glaze) and one at its foot.
- 30 September 2026 : beyond the pale line, on the side where the surface goes down into the dish, there is a **diffuse fringe, 15 to 25 px wide, made of broken orange rust speckles** (#b4622a to #c27a3a) that dissolve irregularly into the green. It is not a smooth gradient: it is dots and short streaks, denser near the wall and disappearing with distance. The opposite side (the high flat surface) has only a very thin fringe.
- 30 September 2026 : the green next to the wall is darker and bluer (cool shadow-like green), then lightens towards the middle of the dish.

## The tile joint

- 30 September 2026 : a **dark hairline of 1 to 2 px** (near black brown), flanked on both sides by a **thin beige line of about 1 px**, and beyond it a **rust speckled fringe 8 to 12 px wide** on the tile edge (same broken orange dots as the arch fringe). The joint is straight, uniform, crisp.

## The glaze

- 30 September 2026 : olive to leaf green (#5b7a3a to #3d5f2a) with a fine directional grain (short streaks) and sparse white micro specks (1 to 2 px, less than 1 per 30 px square). Soft darker and lighter patches at the tile scale.
- 30 September 2026 : reflections are white with a horizontal wave (comb like edge) where the surface is concave.

## What to build from this

- 30 September 2026 : tan clay colour on the whole steep wall, cream hairlines at the top edge and at the foot of the wall, a rust speckle fringe on the floor side of the wall, dark hairline joint with beige hairlines and a rust speckle fringe on the tile edge, fine directional grain on the glaze.
